# THETA AI TRADER Trading Architecture

## Purpose

THETA AI TRADER is an AI-assisted options trading platform built around independent decision engines.

The platform must never rely on a single indicator or a single strategy.

Every trade is the result of multiple intelligence engines working together.

---

# Core Pipeline

Market Data
    ↓
Market Intelligence
    ↓
Market Regime Detection
    ↓
Strategy Intelligence
    ↓
Risk Intelligence
    ↓
Execution Intelligence
    ↓
Adaptive Position Management Engine (APME)
    ↓
Broker Execution
    ↓
Trade Monitoring
    ↓
Analytics & Learning

---

## Engine Philosophy

Every Engine performs one responsibility only.

Examples:

- Market Regime Engine
- Greeks Engine
- Liquidity Engine
- Strategy Intelligence Engine
- Confidence Engine
- Trade Decision Engine
- Risk Manager
- Position Sizing Engine

Engines must be:

- Stateless
- Independent
- Testable
- Deterministic

---

## Decision Philosophy

Never take trades using a single signal.

Every trade is evaluated using multiple dimensions including:

- Trend
- Volatility
- Liquidity
- Option Greeks
- Open Interest
- Market Breadth
- Event Risk
- Strategy Suitability
- Risk Score
- Execution Quality

---

## Strategy Philosophy

Strategies are selected dynamically.

The software decides whether to use:

- Short Strangle
- Iron Condor
- Broken Wing Butterfly
- Jade Lizard
- Bull Put Spread
- Bear Call Spread
- Long Volatility Strategies

based on market conditions.

---

## Risk Philosophy

Capital protection is the highest priority.

When uncertainty is high:

- Reduce position size.
- Avoid low-quality trades.
- Prefer no trade over a poor trade.

---

## Long-Term Vision

The platform should evolve into an institutional-grade automated trading system capable of making intelligent, explainable, and risk-aware decisions.

